  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0416' consists of 10 tables. The primary purpose of this schema is to manage user information, company details, job postings, and user interactions within a platform.\nThe 'User' table holds user information including avatar, email, nickname, password, registration time, role, user ID, and username. The 'Company' table contains details about the company including company address, company ID, company name, company profile, and contact information.\nThe 'Conversation' table is used to manage user conversations, with each conversation identified by a unique conversation ID. The 'Message_Board' table stores messages posted by users, with each message identified by a unique message ID.\nThe 'Job_Info' table contains job posting information, including company ID, content, education level, job category, job info ID, requirements, salary, title, and work location.\nThe 'User_and_Conversation' table is a junction table that links users to conversations, with each record representing a unique conversation between two users. The 'User_and_Message' table is another junction table that links users to messages, with each record representing a unique message sent by a user.\nThe 'Resume_Submission' and 'Resume_Save' tables are used to manage resume submissions and saves, with each record representing a unique submission or save by a user for a specific job posting.\nFinally, the 'Company_and_Job_Info' table is a junction table that links companies to job postings, with each record representing a unique job posting by a company.\nAll tables in this schema allow null values except for the 'User_ID' in the 'User' and 'Company' tables, and the 'User_ID', 'Message_ID', and 'Job_Info_ID' in the 'Message_Board', 'User_and_Message', 'Resume_Submission', and 'Resume_Save' tables. The primary keys of these tables are unique and not null. The foreign keys in the schema enforce referential integrity, ensuring that the relationships between tables are maintained.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThe online job recruitment system mainly serves three types of users: job seekers, companies, and administrators. The system provides the following functionalities:\n1.User Information Management: Each registered user has a unique user ID, username, password, email, avatar, nickname, registration time, and role.\n2.Company Information Management: Each company includes basic information such as company ID, company name, company address, company profile, and contact information.\n3.Job Information Management: Companies can post job openings or save matching resumes from users. Users can view detailed job information and submit resumes to the company. Job information includes job ID, title, content, requirements, job category, salary, education level, and work location.\n4.Conversation Management: Users can communicate via conversations. Conversation details include conversation ID, message content, and send time.\n5.Message Board Management: Users can update the message board with new content. The message board includes message ID, message content, and message time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0416.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0416\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Company` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company_address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `company_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Conversation` (\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`conversation_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Message_Board` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_board_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Job_Info` (\n  `job_info_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `requirements` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `education_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_category` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `work_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_info_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `job_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `Company` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_and_Conversation` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `conversation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_conversation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_conversation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `Conversation` (`conversation_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_and_Message` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_message_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_message_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `Message_Board` (`message_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Resume_Submission` (\n  `submission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_info_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`submission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `resume_submission_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `resume_submission_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_info_id`) REFERENCES `Job_Info` (`job_info_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Resume_Save` (\n  `save_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_info_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`save_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `resume_save_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `resume_save_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_info_id`) REFERENCES `Job_Info` (`job_info_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Company_and_Job_Info` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_info_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`, `job_info_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `company_and_job_info_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `Company` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `company_and_job_info_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_info_id`) REFERENCES `Job_Info` (`job_info_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
